# Cloudflare Pages custom response headers.
# Only the paths listed here are affected; everything else keeps the defaults
# Pages already sends.

# The service worker script must never be served stale. Cloudflare Pages
# defaults static assets to `max-age=14400`, which means a fix deployed to
# /essa/sw.js could take up to four hours to reach an installed app: the
# browser is entitled to reuse its cached copy for that long before it even
# checks for a new one. `no-cache` forces a revalidation on every update check,
# so a new worker is picked up on the next visit.
#
# The page, the manifest and the icons are left alone. The worker is
# network-first, so the HTML is already fetched fresh whenever there is signal.
/essa/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
